## What We Are Building

End-to-end Plan-driven production pipeline for SandyStudio's anchor-chain architecture. The session split into two related arcs:

1. **TD-46/47/50 — Animator pipeline cleanup.** Renamed EXEC-VANIM/VGEN from the duplicate «Animator» label to «Video Designer» / «Video Artist». Fixed the «two videos per shot» bug (TD-47, single-shot vs Pilot Pass). Closed the long-running fast/standard tier switching bug (TD-50) — Polина's `triggerAgent(EXEC-VGEN)` previously routed to legacy `generate-shot` handler which dropped `planAssetId`, causing TD-44's `resolveVanimProviderId` to never see the Plan body. Trigger route now reroutes to `single-shot` when payload has planAssetId; legacy handler also extracts planAssetId for defence-in-depth.

2. **TD-49 Phase 1 + Phase 2 backbone — anchor chain core.** Director's architectural fix for mirror drift between shots: each shot has its OWN start_anchor + end_anchor (different asset_ids, scene-time aligned at match cuts but different camera angles — eliminates jitter by construction). Phase 1 shipped a hard LAYOUT LOCK directive in the EREF Designer prompt that proved sufficient for SH08 mirror anchoring on legacy Plan. Phase 2 backbone shipped the schema + extractor + validator + runner + Critic + approve-route wiring needed for the full anchor pair pipeline. **P2.3 (EREF Designer pair authoring mode) deferred to next session** — that's the LLM-side change that actually produces the IMG-anchor_* assets the backbone gates on. Without P2.3 the pipeline doesn't activate end-to-end.

Master squash commit `a277aaf` (22 files, +1981, -42) — full Phase 2 backbone landed.

