## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Scene_master Bible section approach (commit `eb9cda1`)** — failed because: Director rightly pointed out (`SBL-location_sandy_bedroom_continuity` already exists as LOCKED Bible asset with full LOCATION BIBLE markdown). The new section was duplicate of existing convention. Superseded by TD-49 Phase 1 LAYOUT LOCK prompt update (commit `007628e`) which uses the EXISTING SBL-location image. Commit `eb9cda1` retained for back-compat (harmless dead section) — cleanup deferred.
- **First squash-merge attempt — `git checkout master` in feature worktree** — failed because: `master` is checked out in a separate worktree at `C:/SandyStudio/.claude/worktrees/agitated-lederberg-a292d3`. Git refuses to check out a branch already used by another worktree.
- **`git pull origin master` recovery attempt** — failed because: after the failed checkout I was still on the feature branch, and pull tried to merge origin/master INTO the feature branch, creating live conflicts. Aborted via `git merge --abort`. Right path: use `git -C <master-worktree-path>` to operate in the master worktree.
- **`git stash pop` on feature branch after merge** — partially failed because: `.claude/pa-feedback.log`, `settings.local.json`, `scheduled_tasks.lock` files had conflicting state (probably auto-modified during merge). Stash@{0} retained for safety. Working tree state acceptable (untracked diagnostic scripts restored).
- **Squash-merge initial conflicts (8 unmerged files)** — surfaced because: feature branch is 286 commits ahead of master with 184 auto-sync commits, master had concurrent edits in same files. Resolved by `git checkout --theirs` for all 8 files (feature branch is strict superset of master per merge-base check `0635a25` showing master had no exclusive new commits).
- **Polина's regenerateImageFromPlan didn't activate LAYOUT LOCK** — failed because: it uses the OLD approved plan v03 text (authored before commit `007628e`). To actually test new Designer prompt, need `regenerateRefPlan` (re-author plan), not `regenerateImageFromPlan` (image-only). Documented in concierge thread; Director chose to keep observing.
- **`triggerAgent(EXEC-VGEN)` without planAssetId payload before TD-50** — failed because: routed to legacy `generate-shot` event handler that dropped planAssetId → resolveProvider DB default (Seedance fast) won regardless of Plan declaration. Fixed by TD-50.

