## Decisions Made

- **Pair anchors (different asset_ids) over shared keyframe** — reason: Director's «opening_camera_motion REQUIRED не достаточно» feedback; shared keyframe creates static-static duplicate frame at boundary that even aggressive camera motion can't fully mask. Two paired anchors authored as different angles eliminate jitter by construction.
- **`SBL-location_<slug>` IS the scene_master de facto** — reason: discovering Director already had `SBL-location_sandy_bedroom_continuity` v01 LOCKED with full LOCATION BIBLE text + canonical image. New `SBL-scene_master_*` section was redundant. P2.2's loadAnchorChainContext preference order honours both for forward compat.
- **TD-49 Phase 1 = prompt-level fix, not architectural** — reason: existing pipeline already passes the LOCKED Bible location image as `anchor_assets`. Mirror drift was a prompt-strength issue (Designer didn't emphasize preservation). Hard LAYOUT LOCK directive added to Step 5 prompt template — minimum change, maximum signal.
- **Squash master commit over fast-forward** — reason: feature branch was 286 commits ahead with 184 auto-sync noise commits. Project house pattern (12d708f, ec15493) uses squash for sprint cycles. Loses atomic TD-X commit history on master but feature branch retains them for audit.
- **`git checkout --theirs` to resolve all 9 merge conflicts** — reason: merge-base check showed master had no exclusive commits beyond what's on feature branch (`0635a25` base; master only at `c625830` since base, which is on feature branch too). Feature branch is strict superset. Conflicts were artifacts of auto-sync commits + intermediate state, not real divergence.
- **P2.3 deferred to next session** — reason: it's the LLM-prompt-side change requiring careful Designer prompt design + live test cycles. Better as isolated focused work. Phase 2 backbone (P2.1-P2.6 minus P2.3) is structurally complete and stable as a foundation.
- **TD-50 fix is F1 + F3 (defence-in-depth)** — reason: trigger route reroute (F1) handles the primary case (Polина's manual trigger). Legacy handler also extracts planAssetId (F3) covers future code paths that might emit `generate-shot` directly (replay-pilot fixtures, third-party callers, queued retries). Belt-and-suspenders.

